    "turn_text": "Well, in the bipartisan infrastructure bill, clearly in the Senate, many work together. But that's sort of sitting out there now with all this other work they're doing around it. How do you see this playing out? Do you think they have a formula to make it successful? Because as you say, they have a razor-thin vote margin, despite the fact that they have this notion of mandate.",
