    "turn_text": "Not helpful. Not helpful. And, you know, I've served in both the House and Senate. And I think relationships matter a lot more in the Senate. Now, I was the whip almost the whole time I was in the House. And we had little margins. So I had, I was constantly working to figure out which Democrats could help us on which issues. And I had pretty good relate, I had pretty good bipartisan relationships there. But I think generally, people that come to the Senate from the House and find out that, you know, you do have some dependency on each other because of the rules. Every Senator can slow down things by objecting to not giving consent and relationships really matter. And I think we were all hopeful that after the Reed McConnell relationships at the McConnell Schumer relationships would be better and they don't seem to be.",
